{
  "_what": "does harmony correspond to what a human perceives? 5,500 SCUT faces, each with a mean rating from 60 volunteers.",
  "_gated": "\u00a74.1(a) OVERRIDDEN by calibration_subject 2026-09-09, reversing \u00a76.4 (locked 2026-09-04). Harmony IS gated on rater agreement: Pearson r 95% CI lower bound > 0.1, within cohort, pre-registered BEFORE the correlation was computed. An axis must clear it in EVERY measurable cohort or it is REFUSED.",
  "_what_harmony_now_means": "NOT geometric harmony \u2014 geometry that predicts the ratings of 60 Chinese volunteers aged 18-27. The neoclassical-canon literature no longer applies to it.",
  "_aggregation_is_this_files_choice": "calibration_subject set the bar, not the aggregation across cohorts. The conservative reading is used: an axis must clear it everywhere it is measurable, or it is refused.",
  "_cohort_mapping_is_a_judgement": {
    "Asian -> east_asian": "JUDGEMENT. SCUT is from South China University of Technology; FairFace splits east_asian from southeast_asian and SCUT does not. southeast_asian sensitivity run.",
    "Caucasian -> white": "JUDGEMENT. Closest label; FairFace carries middle_eastern separately.",
    "age": "ASSUMED 20_29 \u2014 SCUT CARRIES NO AGE LABEL. If these faces skew older every percentile is against the wrong band. 30_39 sensitivity run."
  },
  "_coverage": "2 of 7 FairFace race labels, 4 of 62 cohorts, 1 of 4 age bands. This is not coverage of the bank.",
  "_within_cohort": "SCUT's raters are 60 Chinese volunteers aged 18-27 and cross-race ratings differ systematically, so pooling would let rater behaviour masquerade as a geometry-beauty relationship. Every correlation is computed inside one (race x sex) cohort.",
